INT. BABY SHOWER - SUBURBAN LIVING ROOM - DAY

Pastel balloons. A sheet cake. Six guests, one gift table.

                    BEATRIZ
          Open mine first!

                    DOT
          Mine's the big one.

                    CHANTELLE
          Mine's the pretty one.

                    HONEY
          Everybody wait, the cake is melting.

                    BEATRIZ
          It's February.

                    HONEY
          Then why is it melting?

                    CHANTELLE
          Oh my God, that's the heater.

                    DOT
          Who put the cake on the heater?

                    MARGUERITE
          I thought it was a table.

                    BEATRIZ
          Marguerite!

                    MARGUERITE
          It looked like a table!

                    CHANTELLE
          (to the guest of honor)
          Lourdes, say something.

LOURDES (30s, nine months pregnant) stands, grips the arm of the couch, and looks down.

                    LOURDES
          My water just broke.

The room screams. Gifts fly. Beatriz grabs the keys, Dot grabs Lourdes, Chantelle grabs the cake, and Honey grabs a towel. Marguerite stands in the middle of it all.

                    MARGUERITE
          (calmly)
          I'll get the casserole.
